    <diagram name="README" id="6uWCGEVDWqdnvIiDKMtO">
        <mxGraphModel dx="927" dy="709" grid="1" gridSize="10" guides="1" tooltips="1" connect="1" arrows="1" fold="1" page="1" pageScale="1" pageWidth="850" pageHeight="1100" background="#ffffff" math="0" shadow="0">
            <root>
                <mxCell id="WjNtcwFtisM9cXZzO78z-0"/>
                <mxCell id="WjNtcwFtisM9cXZzO78z-1" parent="WjNtcwFtisM9cXZzO78z-0"/>
                <mxCell id="24p901fEKNji1qQnN0xF-50" parent="WjNtcwFtisM9cXZzO78z-1" style="text;html=1;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;fontSize=24;autosize=1;" value="&lt;h4&gt;Directions to Create Your Game Map&lt;/h4&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="50" width="440" x="220" y="21" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
                <mxCell id="24p901fEKNji1qQnN0xF-51" parent="WjNtcwFtisM9cXZzO78z-1" style="text;strokeColor=none;align=left;fillColor=none;html=1;verticalAlign=top;whiteSpace=wrap;rounded=0;" value="&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;1. Revew the example map on the &lt;a href=&quot;data:page/id,E0RcvYQW2tOlB-kFRd9z&quot;&gt;Example&lt;/a&gt; tab to see what your finished map should look like. Your finished Map should look the same except with different map title, room names, item names, and villain name. Do NOT use ths same title and names on your map.&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;2. On the &lt;a href=&quot;data:page/id,BxN_fVSwImqooR-HojqY&quot;&gt;Map&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;tab, replace all &amp;lt;placeholder text&amp;gt;, inlcuding delimiters (&quot;&amp;lt;...&amp;gt;&quot;), with &lt;b&gt;your text&lt;/b&gt; that describes &lt;b&gt;your game world&lt;/b&gt;. All titles and names should be in &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.grammarly.com/blog/sentences/title-case-sentence-case/&quot;&gt;title case&lt;/a&gt;.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;ul&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Map Title&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Room Names&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Item Names&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Villain Name&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;Do &lt;b&gt;NOT&lt;/b&gt; change anything else on the Mab tab.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/ul&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;3. Compare your finished &lt;a href=&quot;data:page/id,BxN_fVSwImqooR-HojqY&quot;&gt;Map&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;with the &lt;a href=&quot;data:page/id,E0RcvYQW2tOlB-kFRd9z&quot;&gt;Example&lt;/a&gt;. Both should look identical except for the title and names.&amp;nbsp; &lt;/span&gt;&lt;i style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;Note&lt;/i&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;: The example map is just an example of what your finished map should look like. Your map must describe your unique, original game world. Do &lt;/span&gt;&lt;b style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;NOT&lt;/b&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt; use the example Dragon-Castle theme in your map.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;background-color: transparent; font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 18px;&quot;&gt;&lt;i&gt;Tip. &lt;/i&gt;After you submit your final Project Two assignment, you can exapand your game world with addtitional rooms, items, and villains. You can also add and remove connections between rooms. For now, just stick with the layout in the provided starter map.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(63, 63, 63); font-size: 18px; background-color: transparent;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
                    <mxGeometry height="560" width="690" x="80" y="120" as="geometry"/>
                </mxCell>
            </root>
        </mxGraphModel>
    </diagram>
